.DS_Store
__pycache__/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
/exports-v3/_*/
*.pyc

# cellucid.prepare() keeps one writer lock beside every export directory it
# rebuilds; the inode outlives the run by design. That design only bounds the
# count while the locked directory name repeats, which is why scripts/pinned_build.py
# stages under one fixed name: a randomly named stage made prepare() lock a name
# that could never recur, and every run left one more lock behind.
/exports-v3/.*.cellucid.lock

# scripts/pinned_build.py takes a second, non-waiting publication lock beside the
# directory it swaps in; a crashed run is what leaves that inode behind.
/exports-v3/.*.publish.lock

# The write-ahead recovery sidecars both publishers place beside the generation
# they replace: cellucid.prepare()'s journal, its atomic-write temporary, and
# its staged and set-aside trees, plus the equivalent pair scripts/pinned_build.py
# creates. One of these surviving a run means an interrupted publication, and
# the argument for leaving them visible was that a human should see that in
# `git status`. They still see it: the generation itself is committed, so an
# interrupted swap shows up as modified or deleted tracked files under
# exports-v3/<id>/, which is a louder signal than an untracked sidecar and does
# not depend on this file. What ignoring them prevents is the failure that has
# no other guard -- a stage or a backup is a complete second copy of the
# generation, tens of thousands of files, that `git add -A` would commit into
# the published catalog and that no suite would sweep, because every suite that
# enumerates exports-v3/ skips hidden entries. An interrupted publication is
# resolved by rerunning the writer, which reads the journal; it is not resolved
# by Git.
/exports-v3/.*.cellucid-transaction.json
/exports-v3/.*.cellucid-transaction.json.tmp
/exports-v3/.*.cellucid-stage-*/
/exports-v3/.*.cellucid-backup-*/
/exports-v3/.*.stage/
/exports-v3/.*.backup-*/

# Tool caches (pytest, mypy, ruff, pytest-benchmark)
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.benchmarks/

# Scratch directories a crashed publisher test can leave behind
.pinned-publish-test-*/
